  <content>
  <section><para>Complete the following questions to practice the skills you have learned in this lesson.</para>
<section class="check-understanding"><exercise data-content-id="92d59337-3613-48cb-ba17-d11f71cb511e"><problem><para>
      <para><emphasis>Select two </emphasis>true statements about the graph that represents \(y=2x(x-11)\).</para>
      </para></problem><solution><para>["Its \\(x\\)-intercepts are at \\((0,0)\\) and \\((11,0)\\).", "The \\(x\\)-coordinate of its vertex is 5.5."]</para><para>
      <para>The correct answers are: Its \(x\)-intercepts are at (0,0) and (11,0). The \(x\)-coordinate of its vertex is 5.5. </para>
    </para></solution></exercise></section></section>
</content>
